  "verbalization": "Ursodeoxycholic Acid (UDCA) is implicated in the pathogenesis of cholecystolithiasis through a cascade of indications that link it to cholelithiasis and cholecystolithiasis. The evidence suggests that UDCA is associated with the formation of gallstones, as it is indicated for cholelithiasis and cholecystolithiasis. This relationship is supported by the indirect pathway where UDCA is linked to cholic acid, which in turn is linked to cholecystolithiasis. The presence of these indications implies a potential role of UDCA in the development or maintenance of gallstone disease, possibly through its effects on bile composition or gallbladder function. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which UDCA may contribute to the formation of cholecystolithiasis, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated."
